## 3. Turn on Remote Lock

If your phone is stolen, Remote Lock lets you lock it from any browser at [android.com/lock](https://www.android.com/lock), using just your phone number. You don't need your Google password, which helps if your passwords are saved on the stolen phone.

**Go to:**
`Settings > Google > All services > Theft protection > Remote Lock`

Turn it on, and add the optional **Security question** so nobody else can lock your phone with only your number. Remote Lock needs the phone to have a SIM, be online and have Find Hub turned on.

