  <img src="/images/blog/settings_remote_lock.jpeg" alt="android.com/lock page asking for the phone number" />
  <figcaption>Remote Lock at android.com/lock</figcaption>
</figure>

## 4. Make sure Find Hub is on

Find Hub (formerly Find My Device) shows where your phone is on a map and lets you ring, lock or erase it from another device at [google.com/android/find](https://www.google.com/android/find).

It's usually on by default when you sign in with a Google account, but check: open Settings and search for "Find Hub". Make sure it's on and that location is allowed.

